Q: react-hook-form - How to correctly type generic UseFormRegister&lt;T&gt; when dealing with sub form? A: <p>Looks like its impossible to avoid using <code>as</code> casting, but to make it more safe you can use this helper:</p>
<pre><code>export function asFieldPath2&lt;TShape extends FieldValues, T extends TShape = TShape&gt;(
  name: Extract&lt;keyof TShape, string&gt;,
): FieldPath&lt;T&gt; {
  return name as unknown as FieldPath&lt;T&gt;;
}
</code></pre>
<p>In my case (I had problems with name) I used it like this in JSX. It does checking of key existence in <strong>FLAT</strong> form structure and then casts to what react hook for expects</p>
<pre><code>name={asFieldPath2&lt;UserDetails, T&gt;('firstName')}
</code></pre>
